{{!
    @template core/credential_notice_email

    Tells someone about a change to a credential they are responsible for, such as a new token or secret.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * logo - The site's compact logo URL, if it has one.
    * sitename - The site name, for the logo's alt text.
    * greeting - The greeting line.
    * message - The sentence naming the credential, leading into the date.
    * expiry - The credential's expiry date and time.
    * action - What to do about it, with a link to the page managing the credential.
    * footer - Why the recipient is receiving this.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "logo": "https://example.com/logo.png",
        "sitename": "Mount Orange School",
        "greeting": "Hello Sam,",
        "message": "A personal access token called \"Attendance export\" was created on your account on Mount Orange School. It expires on",
        "expiry": "13 August 2026, 3:06 PM",
        "action": "If you didn't create it, revoke it now and change your password: <a href=\"#\">Personal access tokens</a>",
        "footer": "This is a security notice, so it can't be turned off."
    }
}}
{{! Styled inline because email clients drop stylesheets and cannot be relied on to honour a media
    query. So the text is capped at a readable width and the logo centred over it. }}
<div style="max-width: 600px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18px">
    {{#logo}}
        <div style="margin-bottom: 10px; text-align: center;">
            <img src="{{{logo}}}" alt="{{sitename}}" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;" />
        </div>
    {{/logo}}
    <p>{{greeting}}</p>
    <p>{{{message}}}</p>
    <h2 style="letter-spacing: 5px;">{{expiry}}</h2>
    <p>{{{action}}}</p>
    <br/>
    <div style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px">
        <p>{{footer}}</p>
    </div>
</div>
